{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2171","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Anisphia Wynn Palettia and Good Permutations"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I've always loved the word magic. It has a way of making people happy, of putting a smile on their faces."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"— Anisphia Wynn Palettia"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Anis and her new assistant Euphie are improving the Witch's Broom! Magicology requires great precision and care — in order to fly, the construction of the broom must have sufficiently few imperfections."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For an arbitrary array $$$a$$$ of length $$$m$$$, call an index $$$i$$$ ($$$1\\leq i\\leq m-2$$$) "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bad"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$a_i$$$, $$$a_{i+1}$$$, and $$$a_{i+2}$$$ are all pairwise coprime. More formally, $$$i$$$ is a bad index if and only if $$$\\gcd(a_i, a_{i+1}) = \\gcd(a_i, a_{i+2}) = \\gcd(a_{i+1}, a_{i+2}) = 1$$$$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$. Furthermore, call $$$a$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if it has at most $$$6$$$ bad indices."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an integer $$$n$$$. Construct a good permutation$$$^{\\text{†}}$$$ $$$p$$$ of length $$$n$$$. It can be shown that such a permutation always exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that you do not have to minimize the number of bad indices."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$$$$\\gcd(x, y)$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_common_divisor"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"greatest common divisor"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{†}}$$$ A permutation of length $$$n$$$ is an array that contains every integer from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ exactly once, in any order."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 10^4$$$)  — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3\\leq n \\leq 2\\cdot 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2\\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output on a single line $$$n$$$ integers $$$p_1, p_2, \\dots, p_n$$$, an example of a good permutation of length $$$n$$$. If there are multiple good permutations, you may output any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sampl